        "original_id": "863e169f-0177-5316-9d7a-d83004cbc5f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David T. Beito, T. R. M. Howard, Medgar Evers, Fannie Lou Hamer\n- Organizations: Regional Council of Negro Leadership\n- Publications: The Wall Street Journal, Harper's Magazine\n- Topics: civil rights, self-help, business ownership, entrepreneurship, biography\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Roosevelt Mason \"T. R. M.\" Howard was born on March 4, 1908, and became an American civil rights leader, fraternal organization leader, entrepreneur, and surgeon.\n- In 1951, T. R. M. Howard founded the Regional Council of Negro Leadership in Mississippi to promote civil rights, self-help, and business ownership.\n- T. R. M. Howard mentored Medgar Evers and Fannie Lou Hamer.\n- T. R. M. Howard died on May 1, 1976.\n- David T. Beito wrote \"Black Maverick,\" a biography of T. R. M. Howard.\n- \"Black Maverick\" describes T. R. M. Howard as a civil rights leader, surgeon, entrepreneur, and self-help advocate.\n- \"Black Maverick\" was reviewed by The Wall Street Journal, Harper's Magazine, and other publications.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
